{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/pulls/448","id":3860245419,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSbOoU87mFqur","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/448","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/448.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/448.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/448","number":448,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Procedural how-to: elaboration-rebind fix + multi-source guide infrastructure (#444)","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Issue #444 — \"Unknown prompt: Can you give me specific instructions?\"\n\nAfter a `procedural_how_to` answer to *\"how to publish to npm\"*, the bare\nelaboration follow-up *\"Can you give me specific instructions?\"* dead-ended at\nthe unknown-intent opener. This PR fixes that coreference bug **and**, following\nthe maintainer's in-PR direction, widens the scope to ship the multi-source\nguide infrastructure the issue also asks for — all in this single PR.\n\n### 1. The coreference fix (R1–R3, R15)\n- **Root cause:** the follow-up carries no \"how to\" lead-in, so\n  `try_how_to_procedure` declined and every later handler fell through. There was\n  no procedural analogue to issue #341's `software_project_followup`. Same gap in\n  the JS worker. (Dispatch passes `prompt.to_lowercase()` with punctuation\n  intact, so the handler re-runs `normalize_prompt` before phrase-matching.)\n- New `procedural_elaboration` seed meaning (`data/seed/meanings-how.lino`,\n  en/ru/hi/zh) with a declared + generated role.\n- New `try_procedural_how_to_followup` handler that recovers the prior how-to\n  turn and rebinds the elaboration to that procedure in the original language;\n  mirrored as `tryProceduralHowToFollowup` in `formal_ai_worker.js` (R15 parity).\n\n### 2. Maintainer follow-up, delivered in this PR (R17–R23)\n- **x10 diverse-topic elaboration tests (R17).** The rebind is covered across\n  12 distinct domains, not just npm publishing.\n- **All external trusted services available (R5/R6/R8, R18).** wikiHow, the\n  Stack Exchange network, the MediaWiki family (Wikibooks/Wikiversity/Wikivoyage),\n  and GitHub READMEs/docs are declared in `data/seed/sources-registry.lino` under\n  an `external_trusted` group, each with an `api` endpoint, license, and cache.\n- **Settings opt-in/opt-out (R19).** Each source carries a `settings_key` and\n  `default_enabled true`; the web settings UI renders a toggle section and the\n  worker skips a service's live fetch when its toggle is `false`.\n- **≥10 benchmark cases from popular AI benchmarks (R20).**\n  `data/benchmarks/procedural-howto-suite.lino` adds representative cases in the\n  style of IFEval, Super-NaturalInstructions, Self-Instruct, OASST1, BIG-bench,\n  and MMLU — across apology letters, meal planning, gardening, bicycle repair,\n  pour-over coffee, and nutrition labels — each with a paraphrased held-out\n  variant, ratcheted by `procedural_howto_benchmarks.rs`.\n- **Central benchmark catalog (R21).** `docs/benchmarks.md` indexes every\n  benchmark suite the repository has ever touched, guarded by\n  `tests/unit/docs_requirements.rs`.\n- **Grounded meta-algorithm (R22/R23).** `data/meta/procedural-howto-recipe.lino`\n  + `docs/meta-algorithm.md` + `tests/unit/specification/meta_algorithm.rs`\n  encode and continuously verify against the live source the eight ordered steps\n  that reproduce this topic's Rust handler — so we learn from our own source code\n  how to produce changes on the topic, not just emit one-off code changes.\n\n### Verification\n- **916 unit tests** green (`cargo test --test unit`), incl. the new benchmark,\n  meta-algorithm grounding, and external-service registry/settings suites, and\n  total reference-closure at zero unresolved tokens.\n- **JS worker parity:** `experiments/check_worker_followup.mjs` (Node `vm`) —\n  recognition in en/ru/zh, negative case, prior-dialogue gate, full rebind, and\n  the new service opt-out behaviour. All checks pass.\n- **e2e:** `tests/e2e/tests/issue-444.spec.js` drives the two-turn flow.\n- **Guards:** `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`,\n  and `check:i18n` / `check:language-test-coverage` / `check:language-parity` /\n  `check:intent-coverage` / `check:web-tdz` all pass.\n\n### Docs / process\nDeep case study in `docs/case-studies/issue-444/`, `Project Conventions` section\nin `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and a `bump: minor` changelog fragment.\n\nCloses #444.\n","created_at":"2026-06-13T15:08:39Z","updated_at":"2026-06-14T00:04:48Z","closed_at":"2026-06-14T00:04:48Z","merged_at":"2026-06-14T00:04:48Z","merge_commit_sha":"c96a81d4a0171924ddcdd89e8c1052fa11a08954","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/oth